  "visualReview": {
    "coverage": "Viewed every page and cover in eight 3×3 contact sheets, then re-viewed every corrected sheet. Full-size final checks: 0169 p08, 0170 p03, 0171 p04 and p06, 0172 p08, 0173 p08, 0174 p08, 0175 p04 and p07, 0176 p05 and p07.",
    "notes": [
      "0169: one shared double rocking chair remains under the red umbrella. Pencil marks change from a tailed circle to an open circle and then a completed puddle/leaf-boat drawing; the drawing bag is closed on the lap at the end. A single broad squirrel tail brushes the mole’s trouser leg; added drops stay at the umbrella edges.",
      "0170: exactly two old red shoes retain white laces and speaking toe mouths. The failed fit leaves the heel outside; socks are removed before the shoes move into the toy cart. Brown new shoes appear outdoors, the father’s hand meets the child’s hand, and the two old shoes remain cart passengers at the music house.",
      "0171: the cat is transparent line artwork on the fogged pane, with rounded ears and four paws. The first clear square is too high; the later round aperture sits beside the eye while the fog beneath the paws remains intact. The reaching pose replaces one grounded paw; the final lying pose remains beside the round window, and foliage hides the snail.",
      "0172: the pig retains pale green dress and brown rain boots, and the grey stone has no limbs. Imagined yellow-hat adventures appear only in a distinct story vignette; the scene progresses to a house and covered bed as the stone’s eyes narrow and close. The wooden stump is visible, and the final boots meet at their toes.",
      "0173: the three active books preserve red train, yellow nine-layer cake, and blue boot covers. They open together, all close, and red/yellow return to the low shelf while only the blue book is read. The final blue book rests beside the pillow without covering the sleeping child’s face; the boot-page mouse has a petal blanket.",
      "0174: the honey-coloured bench keeps four short legs and a curved back with two eyes, nose and mouth. The empty nest stays empty; the single blue flower stays on the seat. Tears remain through the conversation and stop only in the final page; the seated mouse leaves both bench eyes visible as the fireflies appear.",
      "0175: the reserved window chair remains empty while the hedgehog fetches glasses; the rabbit grandmother uses the separate rocking chair. The low wooden box is visible after the unsuccessful seat attempt and later supports warm water. On return, the hedgehog wears glasses, one open bear-and-carrot book is shown, and the dormouse sits with folded legs on the round mat.",
      "0176: all pages preserve the same five white circles in the same order. The mistake is in circle two; the frog demonstrates one-to-three then three-to-five, and the clay child finishes in five with two and four empty. The frog retains three white back spots and a white bow; the final child sits outside the route and the frog returns to the first circle."
    ],
    "limits": "Simplified vector picture-book style. Contact sheets inspect composition and continuity; selected pages enlarged. No claim of bitmap painting, audio QA, browser layout QA or child-user testing."
  },
